From: rhodep port <none@example.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 23:10:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] DIAGNOSTIC: net: ipa: trace the QMI handshake

Not for source= beyond the investigation it belongs to.

The whole driver has three dev_dbg callsites, none of them in ipa_qmi.c,
so there is no way to see how far the AP and the modem get before the SoC
resets. That reset happens when the modem registers on the network with
ipa loaded, and the modem programming its own pipes is on the far side of
this handshake.

Print each step: INDICATION_REGISTER and DRIVER_INIT_COMPLETE arriving
from the modem, the readiness check with the flags it turns on, the AP's
INIT_DRIVER request with the addresses it hands over, and the point where
both sides are ready and the modem netdev starts.

The addresses matter because they are what the modem writes through.
skip_uc_load is printed with them: ipa_qmi_init_driver() derives it from
ipa->uc_loaded, and that flag is left false whenever the microcontroller
reports INIT_COMPLETED while uc_powered is false -- which is what happens
if ipa is loaded after the modem is already up.

Signed-off-by: rhodep port <none@example.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ipa/ipa_qmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ipa/ipa_qmi.c
@@ -125,6 +125,10 @@
 	int ret;
 
 	/* We aren't ready until the modem and microcontroller are */
+	pr_info("ipa-qmi: ready check: modem=%d uc=%d indication_requested=%d sent=%d initial_boot=%d\n",
+		ipa_qmi->modem_ready, ipa_qmi->uc_ready,
+		ipa_qmi->indication_requested, ipa_qmi->indication_sent,
+		ipa_qmi->initial_boot);
 	if (!ipa_qmi->modem_ready || !ipa_qmi->uc_ready)
 		return;
 
@@ -142,6 +146,7 @@
 
 	/* We're ready.  Start up normal operation */
 	ipa = container_of(ipa_qmi, struct ipa, qmi);
+	pr_info("ipa-qmi: both sides ready, starting modem netdev\n");
 	ret = ipa_modem_start(ipa);
 	if (ret)
 		dev_err(ipa->dev, "error %d starting modem\n", ret);
@@ -185,6 +190,8 @@
 	ipa_qmi = container_of(qmi, struct ipa_qmi, server_handle);
 	ipa = container_of(ipa_qmi, struct ipa, qmi);
 
+	pr_info("ipa-qmi: <- INDICATION_REGISTER from modem\n");
+
 	rsp.rsp.result = QMI_RESULT_SUCCESS_V01;
 	rsp.rsp.error = QMI_ERR_NONE_V01;
 
@@ -214,6 +221,8 @@
 	ipa_qmi = container_of(qmi, struct ipa_qmi, server_handle);
 	ipa = container_of(ipa_qmi, struct ipa, qmi);
 
+	pr_info("ipa-qmi: <- DRIVER_INIT_COMPLETE from modem\n");
+
 	rsp.rsp.result = QMI_RESULT_SUCCESS_V01;
 	rsp.rsp.error = QMI_ERR_NONE_V01;
 
@@ -249,6 +258,7 @@
 };
 
 /* Handle an INIT_DRIVER response message from the modem. */
+/* DIAGNOSTIC */
 static void ipa_client_init_driver(struct qmi_handle *qmi,
 				   struct sockaddr_qrtr *sq,
 				   struct qmi_txn *txn, const void *decoded)
@@ -331,6 +341,13 @@
 	req.ctrl_comm_dest_end_pt =
 		ipa->name_map[IPA_ENDPOINT_AP_MODEM_RX]->endpoint_id;
 
+	pr_info("ipa-qmi: -> INIT_DRIVER hdr=[%#x..%#x] v4rt=%#x v6rt=%#x v4flt=%#x v6flt=%#x modem=[%#x +%#x] ctrl_ep=%u skip_uc=%u\n",
+		req.hdr_tbl_info.start, req.hdr_tbl_info.end,
+		req.v4_route_tbl_info.start, req.v6_route_tbl_info.start,
+		req.v4_filter_tbl_start, req.v6_filter_tbl_start,
+		req.modem_mem_info.start, req.modem_mem_info.size,
+		req.ctrl_comm_dest_end_pt, req.skip_uc_load);
+
 	/* skip_uc_load_valid and skip_uc_load are set above */
 
 	mem = ipa_mem_find(ipa, IPA_MEM_MODEM_PROC_CTX);
